### Granot lifecycle reads and Booking/Release commands

- Case/discrepancy implementation paths remain under `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle` (`cases/[caseId]`, `discrepancies`). The old queue, Health, and forensic job URLs redirect. Booking and cancellation review for the Owner lives at `/intakes`. Choosing a waiting intake stays on `/intakes?case=` and does not jump to `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle/cases/:id`. `IntakeCasePage` fetches the case once and routes it: `kind:"booking"` gets `BookingIntakeWorkbench`; `kind:"release"` gets `CancellationIntakeWorkbench`.
- **The booking intake reads as one story, in this order**, and new work belongs in whichever act it answers: (1) *What Granot sent us* — `GranotBookingStatementCard` renders the readable customer/move/money facts produced by `granot-statement-reading.ts`, the priority sentence, then the exact Granot message and Vantage's reading of it behind two drawers; (2) *Who this booking is for* — `MatchedCustomerSection` shows the matched lead, its confidence, Form submitted vs Granot via `intake-known-contacts` (chip, cards, cycle/search strings from `intake-copy`), a collapsible full-lead snapshot, and opens `LeadCandidateBrowser` when the Owner says the customer is wrong; (3) official Booking work — compact official-**Booking**-now strip from the live **Booking** (never Granot), then `BookingOwnerActions` with `surface="intakes"` (never mounts **Confirm Granot Cancellation**; technical `/ingestion/granot/lifecycle` may still). Ban **Finish booking** / **Finish the booking**; (4) the reference drawers from `intake-reference.tsx` (what Vantage already has, every Granot update, the job lifecycle timeline), opened by default only when commands are unavailable. Booking `/intakes` rows and the technical booking case page render the same statement folded into `GranotBookingStatementAccordion`. List and Overview waiting cards use `IntakeCardActions` (postures and list **No Action** above).
- **The cancellation intake is the same first and last acts**, without a customer-matching step: (1) *What Granot sent us* — the same statement card, preferring the latest Release evidence; (2) *Finish the cancellation* — `ReleaseOwnerActions`; (3) the same reference drawers. Cancellation `/intakes` rows and the technical release case page fold the same statement into `GranotBookingStatementAccordion` with `kind="cancellation"`.
- Who a booking is for is answered by `useMatchedLead(caseId)`, not by the form. It derives `chosenLead ?? pickBestCandidate(...)` during render — never from an effect — and shares one `queryKeys.granotLifecycle.candidates(caseId, { scope: "source" })` cache entry with the search panel, so the match costs no extra request. `BookingCommandForm` takes the answer as a `matchedLead` prop and asks only for the official numbers (one Binder amount, Primary Agent, optional Secondary Agent with `No split`, deposit, merchant from the Operations Registry catalog; derived split is read-only). Confirm, update, and referral official details send `primary_agent_id`, optional `secondary_agent_id`, and `total_binder_amount` via `lib/booking/officialBookingDetails.ts` — not per-agent binder rows or Add Agent. `CaseDetail` no longer chooses between a browser and a form: its caller composes one `ownerWork` node.
- `LeadCandidateResults` rows render full lead facts via `candidate-lead-facts.tsx`, and stay read-only (no selection controls) when `onSelect` is absent. `isAllowedIntakeReturn` allows `/intakes` plus safe `/intakes?...` query strings (no `://` or `//`); the technical case page may use that back-link. `/ingestion/granot` redirects to Automations → Granot updates (doc 17).Live Events (`/live-events`, `/ingestion/granot/live`) and the Receipts search were retired by SLIM-02 and show not-found; `/granot-lifecycle` and `/granot-lifecycle/receipts` redirect to Health. `/granot-lifecycle/health` is Owner/Admin read-only (`queryKeys.granotLifecycle.health()`), linked from the sidebar and from Daily dead-letter cards.
- **Owner-visible strings live in `components/intakes/intake-copy.ts`, never inline in an intake component.** The reader owns a moving company: say what happened, then what to do; never print a `snake_case` identifier or name a system he does not operate; every non-working state states whether anything is being lost.
- Browser code always uses the signed `/api/proxy/api/v1/...` boundary. Standard lifecycle GETs (including `operations/health`) are Owner/Admin at the proxy; candidates, creating-observation and every command are Owner-only. Standard/Referral create, update, cancellation, No Action, and Connect Booking to Lead forward `Idempotency-Key`; browser secrets and actor headers are stripped before trusted headers are minted.
- Server DTOs remain semantic authority for source scope, matching, candidate eligibility, masking, timeline ordering, and operations health. Admin components render those DTOs and never open operational Mongo or recompute due work, p95, rates, or alerts.
- `queryKeys.granotLifecycle` is isolated from Employee Booking reconciliation and Granot Automation. `invalidateGranotLifecycleCommandViews` is invoked after Confirm Granot Booking, Update Existing Booking, and No Action (success and `409` refetch), and after Connect Booking to Lead success (`queryKeys.granotLifecycle.connectCandidates` plus booking list/detail). Health uses `queryKeys.granotLifecycle.health()` and is not part of that command invalidation set.
- Live Owner command UI: open standard and Referral Booking cases use `booking-owner-actions`. Owner `/intakes` workbench passes `surface="intakes"` (no **Confirm Granot Cancellation**); the technical case page defaults to `technical`. Referral create starts with blank official fields and never shows candidate/attach controls. Open `kind:"release"`, `mode:"release"` cases use `release-owner-actions` for Create Cancellation, full Update Existing Booking, and No Action. All surfaces require server capabilities and explicit review before submit.
- Polling (case detail 15s) may refresh evidence and timelines but must preserve component-owned confirm/update/cancellation/No Action draft state. Booking replacement initializes once from the live Booking projection (including active catalog IDs), while Cancellation starts blank; neither uses Granot evidence as official defaults. `409` refetch preserves unsent values and never auto-resubmits. Booking and Release discriminants, sequences, and timeline entries never collapse. Release command capability follows the server gate; discrepancies remain false.

## Ownership Boundaries

- **Admin owns:** login/sessions, admin users and invites, UI, route handlers, TanStack Query, frontend constants, signed proxy BFF, public employee-booking nonce.
- **Main server owns:** operational DBs, business rules, sheet sync, analytics, registry, ingestion, Granot automation, Granot lifecycle, reporting delivery, Google Drive connection, reconciliation, exports.
- Do not open `vantagemovers` from admin. (`vantagemovershistorical` was dropped by the 2026-10-04 slimming purge.)
- Legacy CPL is the read-only Old rate book under Setup → Lead costs (`/setup/lead-costs?view=old`). Durable source / lead cost / agent / merchant edits live in the other Setup sections. `/settings` is a permanent redirect, not a parallel surface.
- Mutations must invalidate the relevant query keys (lists, details, search, analytics, registry, reporting) where data can change.

## Quality Practices

- Keep secrets/Mongo/auth in `server/` or route handlers — never in client components.
- Validate proxy paths stay under `VANTAGE_API_BASE_URL`; reject absolute/`://` targets.
- CLI Admin Previews do not inherit branch-only env. When the API host is a protected Preview, set Preview-only `VANTAGE_API_PROTECTION_BYPASS` to the **server** project's automation bypass (never this project's `VERCEL_AUTOMATION_BYPASS_SECRET`) and pass both values with `vercel deploy --env`. Do not set the bypass on Production Admin.
- Do not write audit rows: SLIM-08 removed the Admin Audit Log, and the production purge dropped `admin_audit_logs` on 2026-10-04 (`tests/retired-destinations.test.ts` guards this). Forward CSV/export proxy responses without masking successful backend responses.
- Prefer small focused modules in the owning feature folder.
- After substantive changes: `pnpm lint`, `pnpm typecheck`, and relevant tests.

## Outreach Desk (`/outreach-desk`, Sales Outreach Desk; Numbers + RingCentral Accounts live here)

Packet: `docs/sales-outreach-desk/` (server copy canonical). The server DTO is the authority; the admin renders server decisions only (no cadence, overdue, ranking or authorization in the browser). Evidence: `docs/sales-outreach-desk/workspace/evidence/{A1,A2,ADMIN-SUMMARY}.md`.

- Route: `app/(desk)/outreach-desk/{layout,page,desk-client}.tsx` + `session.ts` — its own route group and "Lead outreach" shell, outside the Admin `DashboardShell`. `?view=team|my|activity|settings` plus Owner-only `numbers|accounts`; `&lead=<subject_id>` selection; `agent=<id>` lets an Owner/Manager open one rep's My view. `components/outreach-desk/data/desk-url.ts` canonicalizes per role and redirects anything else. Owner and Manager default to Team, Rep to My.
- Roles: Owner, Manager (new, IMPL-03) and Rep. A generic Admin has no desk (layout redirects to `/`, BFF refuses). A Manager's only pages are `/outreach-desk` and `/daily`; the edge guard sends a Manager or Rep anywhere else to `/outreach-desk`.
- Look: the route-scoped desk token set `components/outreach-desk/styles/outreach-desk.css` (`.od-*` under `.od-root`, Plus Jakarta Sans via `--font-od`), reproducing `docs/sales-outreach-desk/references/*.webp`. Do not restyle it like the Admin dashboard, and do not reuse it outside the desk.
- Views: `components/outreach-desk/views/` — `team-view.tsx` (four cards, Operations today strip, Daily call goals, Leads needing attention, lead drawer), `my-view.tsx` (goal card, tabs, Needs contact / All active, search, move date, sort, queue, lead panel), `lead-panel.tsx`, `activity-view.tsx`, `settings-view.tsx` (Owner controls/roster/closures/restrictions/enrollment; Manager attendance), `desk-frame.tsx` (capabilities gate, unavailable states). Copy only in `outreach-desk-copy.ts`; display helpers in `lib/format.ts` (null = Pending, never 0; relative times from `as_of`). Server codes are never shown raw: review reasons read "Needs review: <reason>" from `lead.reviewReasons`, explanation codes/values from `lead.explanation` / `projectionStates` / `engineStates`; a code without copy falls back ("Needs review", "Pending" or no line) and is reported through `lib/unknown-codes.ts` (logged once in development). A channel with `verification.state: "unverified"` (a passed deadline capture can't prove yet) reads "Due — not yet verified (activity known through <time>)" in amber via `isUnverified` / `verificationNote` / `rowOverdue` — never overdue, red or a negative countdown; a `pending` channel or row is evidence uncertainty ("Pending — checking call and SMS records"), not "Needs review". Freshness chip tooltips add the server's `reason` in words (`freshness.reasons` via `freshnessReasonText`; a RingCentral error code or any unlisted code reads `reasonFallback` and is reported); a rep count with `actual_basis: "no_activity_recorded"` is a real 0 with the `repZeroActivityTitle` tooltip.
- Data: `lib/api/salesOutreach.ts` (non-strict Zod mirror of the server DTOs, fetch helpers, `SalesOutreachApiError`; read enums the server may grow are tolerant — `SALES_OUTREACH_TOLERATED_ENUMS`, unknown value → safe fallback or kept as text, logged in dev; the configuration value is loose at every level so the Settings PATCH, built in `components/outreach-desk/lib/configuration-patch.ts`, sends back every key it does not know; a body the mirror can't read throws `READ_SHAPE_MISMATCH` and views render it via `ReadFailure`, never as endless skeletons), `lib/query/salesOutreach.ts` (keys, live-frame invalidation, `clearSubject` on 403/404), `components/outreach-desk/data/use-desk-{reads,commands,live,url}.ts`. Every write sends an Idempotency-Key and the server revision.
- BFF: `server/auth/outreach-desk-routes.ts` holds the exact Rep/Manager method+path allowlists (server S1 handoff); the generic proxy forwards desk `Idempotency-Key`, pins `scope=production` and carries the server refusal `code`. Live: `app/api/outreach-desk-live/route.ts` → `server/outreach-desk-live.ts` (one EventSource; connect/reconnect/clock = full refetch; 30 s poll only while the stream is down; hidden page closes it; NY-midnight refetch). The generic proxy never forwards the desk stream.
- Mock mode (local only): `OUTREACH_DESK_MOCK=desk|m1` makes the BFF answer desk calls from `tests/outreach-desk/fixtures/synthetic.ts` (`server/outreach-desk-mock.ts`); ignored when `VERCEL_ENV=production`. `tests/outreach-desk/fixtures/server/` are byte copies of the server's `docs/sales-outreach-desk/workspace/evidence/dto-examples/`, re-copied after every server DTO landing; the drift guard in `lib/api/salesOutreach.test.ts` round-trips each one (one READ_RULE per file prefix). Browser checks: `pnpm test:e2e` (Playwright, 1186×742, local e2e users in the csi01 replica).
- Numbers and RingCentral Accounts: today's components (`components/sales-intelligence/numbers/`, `reps.tsx`, …) mounted client-only in the desk shell; their URL state (`components/sales-intelligence/data/url-state.ts`) writes `view=numbers` / `view=accounts` under `/outreach-desk` and still reads an old `view=reps`. Live stays on `app/api/sales-intelligence-live` (Owner only).
- Old links: `/sales-intelligence` and `/sales-intelligence/legacy` are permanent redirects (`legacySalesIntelligenceHref`): `?number=<id>` → `?view=numbers&number=<id>`, `view=reps` → `view=accounts`, any other old query → the desk default. `RepFrame` / `RepUnavailable` are gone.
- Retired (do not rebuild from history): the old Sales Intelligence Outreach desk, Needs Attention, Closed, Overview, Guide, Coverage view, settings form, rep desk, dev gallery, analyses, findings, Case File, conversations/transcripts/audio.
